# MC-X-F12 (writer 9): rate's table governs 2027.., so it is law-dated, and an ask line that reads it directly
# states law (L §4.3 Where a chain ends, an ask line; LOAD-LAWDATE).
=== m.tally
model p
  tally 2
  on 2027-12-31
  start 2027-01-01
  end 2027-12-31

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
source act "the act"

input age3: int
band rate(a: int): money PLN
ask q: rate(age3)

version v_act
  cite act
  governs 2027..
  known 2026-12-01
  age3 = 3 governs always "the age"
  rate: [0, 6) = 400.00 PLN "under 6"
  rate: [6, 18) = 250.00 PLN "6 to 17"
=== expect
refused: LOAD-LAWDATE ask q reads law-dated rate directly, without law (m.tally:12)
